---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import AsideNav from '../../components/AsideNav.astro';
const path = '/about-us/our-clients';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'About Us', href: '/about-us' },
  { name: 'Our Clients', href: path },
];
---
<Base
  title="Our Clients: Government, Finance, MNCs and SMEs"
  description="Public and private organizations trust Databyte Solution with end-of-life data sanitization and disposal, including MNCs, tertiary institutions, schools and healthcare organizations."
  path={path}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <PageHero crumbs={crumbs} eyebrow="Our clients" title="Our Clients" lead="Public and private organizations trust us with their information systems' end-of-life data sanitization and disposal." />
  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="wrap with-aside">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="lead">
          Our satisfied clients include public and private organizations, for example Coca-Cola, ExxonMobil, Fujifilm, tertiary
          institutions, MOE schools and healthcare organizations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every organization has its own data sanitization and internal compliance needs. Databyte Solution works with each client and
          partner to set the best practices and processes for their needs, while keeping the data sanitization process secure and
          auditable.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=databyte+solution#lrd=0x31da11ae48ccabe9:0x2fa65839038454fb,1,,," rel="noopener">Read our reviews on Google →</a></p>

        <h2>Government agencies and financial institutions</h2>
        <p>
          Government agencies' information systems usually hold the most valuable information for malicious parties, as the data is
          often classified and not for public access. Agencies such as defence forces, healthcare organizations and economic agencies
          can hold highly sensitive information that must never leave organizational control. They usually require onsite destruction
          of storage media, performed by in-house staff or by trusted third-party vendors such as Databyte Solution.
        </p>
        <p>
          Financial institutions are deeply intertwined with the economy, and financial information such as bank account details and
          statements is extremely sensitive and valuable. All financial institutions should at least purge or destroy their storage
          media at the end of its useful life.
        </p>

        <h2>Multinational companies</h2>
        <p>
          Large multinational companies often hold large amounts of corporate information: financial information, employee data,
          commercial contracts, and sensitive supplier and pricing information. If breached, it could damage these companies and their
          business partners in the hands of competitors or malicious parties.
        </p>

        <h2>Small and medium businesses</h2>
        <p>
          SMEs make up most businesses in most economies, but they are also the most vulnerable to data breaches, as they usually have
          limited IT resources for data security. That does not remove the need to dispose of used storage media and IT equipment
          securely. With lower volumes of media, SMEs usually send their storage media offsite for sanitization.
        </p>

        <h2>Other organizations</h2>
        <p>Databyte Solution serves organizations of all sizes, private and public.</p>
        <p>
          Every organization should, at a minimum, zero-overwrite or Secure Erase the storage in devices leaving its control. Single-pass
          overwriting with zeros, ATA / SCSI / NVMe Secure Erase and Cryptographic Erase all protect data before storage media is
          disposed of.
        </p>
        <p>
          Organizations can also educate staff on cyber security and put simple controls in place: user access controls, timely
          software updates and patching, scheduled backups, strong passwords, two-factor authentication and drive encryption, among
          many other measures.
        </p>
        <p>Read our <a href="/data-sanitization/guide-to-data-sanitization">Guide to Data Sanitization</a> for more information.</p>
      </article>
      <AsideNav section="/about-us" path={path} />
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
